WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.466
Let's do a few together.

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.034
Problem 1.

00:00:03.599 --> 00:00:10.975
A shelf is an L: a rectangle 10 feet by 8 feet, with a 4 foot by 4 foot corner missing.

00:00:11.633 --> 00:00:12.566
Let's split it.

00:00:12.957 --> 00:00:14.388
I'll cut straight across.

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:17.651
The bottom part is 10 feet by 4 feet.

00:00:18.054 --> 00:00:19.497
That's 40 square feet.

00:00:20.051 --> 00:00:24.443
The top part is 10 minus 4, 6 feet long, and 4 feet tall.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.649
That's 24 square feet.

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:30.027
40 plus 24 is 64 square feet.

00:00:30.825 --> 00:00:31.827
Problem 2.

00:00:32.311 --> 00:00:33.580
Your turn first.

00:00:34.261 --> 00:00:36.378
Pause the video and try this one.

00:00:36.955 --> 00:00:38.700
Then press play and check.

00:00:39.497 --> 00:00:45.364
A tabletop is 14 inches by 8 inches, with a square hole, 5 inches on each side.

00:00:46.011 --> 00:00:51.401
The whole tabletop is 14 times 8, 112 square inches.

00:00:52.048 --> 00:00:56.208
The hole is 5 times 5, 25 square inches.

00:00:56.866 --> 00:01:02.605
Take it away: 112 minus 25 is 87 square inches.

00:01:03.251 --> 00:01:04.219
Problem 3.

00:01:04.772 --> 00:01:06.018
Watch out for this one.

00:01:06.676 --> 00:01:11.568
A picture is 6 inches by 4 inches, with a border 2 inches wide.

00:01:12.342 --> 00:01:14.970
Someone wrote the outside is 8 by 6.

00:01:15.187 --> 00:01:17.071
But the border is on both sides.

00:01:17.427 --> 00:01:19.881
2 plus 6 plus 2 is 10.

00:01:20.469 --> 00:01:22.992
2 plus 4 plus 2 is 8.

00:01:23.581 --> 00:01:26.127
The whole is 10 times 8, 80.

00:01:26.727 --> 00:01:28.426
The picture is 24.

00:01:29.026 --> 00:01:33.117
The border is 80 minus 24, 56 square inches.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:36.367
Add the border on both sides first.
